# Experiment 5 — CNN Training, Optimization & Transfer Learning

## Objective
Systematically study the impact of **weight initialization**, **regularization**, **optimization algorithms**, **CNN hyperparameters**, **transfer learning**, **fine-tuning**, and **5-fold cross-validation** on fine-grained image classification using an ImageNet-pretrained **MobileNetV2** backbone on the **Oxford-IIIT Pet dataset**.

## Architectural & Algorithmic Concepts

| Architecture / Component | Main Idea | Key Insight / Role |
|---|---|---|
| **MobileNetV2** | Lightweight CNN built on inverted residuals and linear bottlenecks | Drastically reduces FLOPs and parameter count without sacrificing representation power. |
| **Depthwise Separable Conv** | Splits standard convolution into depthwise ($K \times K \times 1$) and pointwise ($1 \times 1 \times C$) layers | Reduces computational cost by roughly $\frac{1}{N} + \frac{1}{K^2}$ compared to standard convolution. |
| **He Initialization** | Variance scaling $\sigma^2 = \frac{2}{n_{\text{in}}}$ tailored for rectifiers | Prevents vanishing/exploding activations across ReLU/ReLU6 layers; outperforms Zero, Random, and Xavier. |
| **Batch Normalization** | Mini-batch activation normalization with learnable $\gamma$ scale and $\beta$ shift | Produces zero-centered, unit-scaled activations; smooths the loss landscape and accelerates convergence[cite: 1, 2]. |
| **Adam Optimizer** | Combines first-order momentum with second-order adaptive learning rates[cite: 1, 2] | Delivers faster convergence, lower loss, and shorter training time than plain SGD[cite: 1, 2]. |
| **Two-Stage Transfer Learning** | Feature extraction (frozen base) followed by partial fine-tuning[cite: 1, 2] | Fine-tuning unfreezes top layers at a low learning rate ($10^{-5}$) to prevent catastrophic forgetting[cite: 1, 2]. |

## What I Did
- Preprocessed the 37-class Oxford-IIIT Pet dataset by resizing images to $224 \times 224 \times 3$ and normalizing pixels to $[-1, 1]$.
- Built an input pipeline using `tf.data` with parallel mapping, deterministic shuffling, batching, and memory prefetching.
- Froze the ImageNet-pretrained **MobileNetV2** convolutional base and attached a classification head[cite: 1, 2].
- Evaluated 4 initialization schemes on the classifier head: **Zero, Random Normal, Glorot/Xavier, and He**[cite: 1, 2].
- Assessed 4 regularization techniques: **No Regularization, L2 Weight Decay ($10^{-4}$), Dropout ($0.5$), and Batch Normalization**[cite: 1, 2].
- Benchmarked 4 optimization algorithms: **SGD, Momentum ($\beta = 0.9$), RMSProp, and Adam**[cite: 1, 2].
- Ran single-variable sensitivity sweeps across learning rate ($10^{-3}$ vs. $10^{-4}$), batch size ($16, 32, 64$), and dropout ($0.2$ vs. $0.5$).
- Unfroze the top **20 layers** of MobileNetV2 and fine-tuned them using a reduced learning rate of $10^{-5}$.
- Performed **5-fold cross-validation** across the training/validation partition to select the most reliable configuration[cite: 1, 2].
- Retrained the winning configuration on the full development split and conducted a single final evaluation on the untouched test set[cite: 1, 2].

## Dataset
**Oxford-IIIT Pet Dataset**[cite: 1, 2]
- **Total Images:** 7,349 images across 37 cat and dog breeds[cite: 1, 3]
- **Development Set (`trainval.txt`):** 3,680 images (2,944 train / 736 validation)
- **Independent Test Set (`test.txt`):** 3,669 images (strictly held out until final testing)[cite: 1, 2, 3]
- **Spatial Dimensions:** $224 \times 224 \times 3$[cite: 1, 2]
- **Normalization:** $\tilde{x} = \frac{x}{127.5} - 1.0$

## Transfer Learning Workflow

```text
ImageNet-Pretrained MobileNetV2
               ↓
          Freeze Base (154 layers)
               ↓
    Attach New Classification Head (GlobalAvgPool + Dense)[cite: 1, 2]
               ↓
     Train Head Only (Adam, lr = 1e-3)
               ↓
    Unfreeze Top 20 Layers of Base
               ↓
     Fine-Tune End-to-End (lr = 1e-5)
               ↓
5-Fold Cross-Validation Model Selection[cite: 1, 2]
               ↓
  Retrain Best Model on Full TrainVal[cite: 1, 2]
               ↓
 Final Benchmark on Untouched Test Set[cite: 1, 2]
